{"workingDirectory":"/Users/fanysmacpro/Developer/agents/pe6203-agent-harness-safety/results/raw/evidence-contrastive-pilot-ready-20261102/cells/cell-005/run/workspace","projectId":"5ce92af5-1768-4313-858b-f55e1c6828ea","parentId":"f38182fb-527a-48e9-827a-39114e50c3ce","name":"2.1 Build CSV ingestion reader with encoding and delimiter detection","details":"Implement the first stage of the customer pipeline: discover CSV files in the landing zone, read them robustly, and emit raw rows with source metadata.

Handle: BOM/UTF-8/UTF-16/Latin-1 detection, delimiter sniffing (comma/semicolon/tab), quoted fields with embedded delimiters and newlines, header normalization, and streaming reads so large files do not load fully into memory. Tag every row with file name, row number, and ingestion batch id for traceability.

Done when all well-formed and adversarial CSV fixtures from 1.4 parse or fail with an explicit, actionable error.","tags":["csv","ingestion","backend"],"priority":9,"complexity":5,"estimatedHours":12}

{"workingDirectory":"/Users/fanysmacpro/Developer/agents/pe6203-agent-harness-safety/results/raw/evidence-contrastive-pilot-ready-20261102/cells/cell-005/run/workspace","projectId":"5ce92af5-1768-4313-858b-f55e1c6828ea","parentId":"f38182fb-527a-48e9-827a-39114e50c3ce","name":"2.2 Implement schema validation and reject quarantine","details":"Validate ingested rows against the CustomerRecord schema from 1.2. Keep valid rows flowing; route invalid rows to a quarantine store with the specific failure reason (missing required field, bad type, unparseable date, out-of-range value) and source coordinates.

Design it as row-level validation so one bad row never fails a whole file. Produce a per-batch report: rows read, accepted, rejected, and top rejection reasons. Define the policy for unknown extra columns (warn and keep vs. drop).

Done when a batch report is emitted for every ingestion and every rejection reason is individually asserted in tests.","tags":["validation","data-quality","backend"],"priority":9,"complexity":5,"estimatedHours":10}

{"workingDirectory":"/Users/fanysmacpro/Developer/agents/pe6203-agent-harness-safety/results/raw/evidence-contrastive-pilot-ready-20261102/cells/cell-005/run/workspace","projectId":"5ce92af5-1768-4313-858b-f55e1c6828ea","parentId":"f38182fb-527a-48e9-827a-39114e50c3ce","name":"2.4 Compute customer metrics and cohort aggregates","details":"Implement the metric logic from the catalog (1.1) over deduplicated customer records: active/new/returning counts, retention and churn cohorts by signup month, revenue per customer, and segment breakdowns.

Treat this as a pure transformation: deduplicated records in, MetricPoints out. Keep it deterministic and unit-testable with hand-computed expected values on small fixtures. Parameterize the time window rather than hardcoding dates, and handle partial-period edge cases explicitly.

Done when each customer metric has a unit test asserting exact expected values.","tags":["metrics","aggregation","backend"],"priority":9,"complexity":5,"estimatedHours":12}

{"workingDirectory":"/Users/fanysmacpro/Developer/agents/pe6203-agent-harness-safety/results/raw/evidence-contrastive-pilot-ready-20261102/cells/cell-005/run/workspace","projectId":"5ce92af5-1768-4313-858b-f55e1c6828ea","parentId":"f38182fb-527a-48e9-827a-39114e50c3ce","name":"2.5 Load customer records and metrics into the analytical store","details":"Persist deduplicated customer records and computed MetricPoints into the shared analytical store so the dashboard can query them.

Implement idempotent upserts keyed on customer id and (metric id, dimensions, time bucket) so re-running a batch does not double-count — this is the most common source of wrong dashboards. Add batch-level transactional semantics: a failed load leaves no partial state. Version rows by ingestion batch for traceability and rollback.

Done when re-running the same batch twice yields identical row counts and metric values.","tags":["storage","load","backend"],"priority":8,"complexity":4,"estimatedHours":12}

{"workingDirectory":"/Users/fanysmacpro/Developer/agents/pe6203-agent-harness-safety/results/raw/evidence-contrastive-pilot-ready-20261102/cells/cell-005/run/workspace","projectId":"5ce92af5-1768-4313-858b-f55e1c6828ea","parentId":"d37c5c84-91c0-430b-9a88-0f3e4783af72","name":"3.1 Build log source ingestion and format detection","details":"Read application logs from their source (files/log shipper/stream) and determine the format of each record before parsing.

Detect per-line or per-record: JSON vs. plaintext, common plaintext layouts (timestamp-level-service-message), multiline stack traces that must be joined to the preceding error line, and interleaved concurrent request streams. Handle large files by streaming and track offsets/checkpoints so a restart resumes rather than reprocesses.

Emit raw records with source metadata (file, offset, ingestion batch). Done when mixed-format fixtures are each correctly classified and multiline traces are reassembled intact.","tags":["logs","ingestion","backend"],"priority":9,"complexity":5,"estimatedHours":14}

{"workingDirectory":"/Users/fanysmacpro/Developer/agents/pe6203-agent-harness-safety/results/raw/evidence-contrastive-pilot-ready-20261102/cells/cell-005/run/workspace","projectId":"5ce92af5-1768-4313-858b-f55e1c6828ea","parentId":"d37c5c84-91c0-430b-9a88-0f3e4783af72","name":"3.2 Parse raw log records into the canonical LogEvent schema","details":"Convert detected raw records into the LogEvent schema from 1.2: timestamp (normalized to UTC), level, service, message, exception type/stack, request/trace id, status code, and duration.

Write one parser adapter per format plus a timestamp-format fallback chain (ISO8601, epoch seconds/millis, common locale formats). Records that cannot be parsed must land in an `unparsed` bucket with the raw payload preserved — never silently dropped. Extract structured fields from message text with a conservative, documented regex set.

Done when every fixture line maps to either a fully populated LogEvent or a logged parse failure with a reason.","tags":["parsing","logs","backend"],"priority":9,"complexity":6,"estimatedHours":14}

{"workingDirectory":"/Users/fanysmacpro/Developer/agents/pe6203-agent-harness-safety/results/raw/evidence-contrastive-pilot-ready-20261102/cells/cell-005/run/workspace","projectId":"5ce92af5-1768-4313-858b-f55e1c6828ea","parentId":"d37c5c84-91c0-430b-9a88-0f3e4783af72","name":"3.3 Classify errors and group them into signatures","details":"Turn individual error events into groupings an operator can act on.

Normalize each error message into a stable signature by masking variable parts: UUIDs, numeric ids, timestamps, durations, IPs, file paths, and query parameters. Group by (service, exception type, signature) so "user 8821 not found" and "user 9202 not found" collapse together. Assign severity from level plus exception class, and detect first-seen / last-seen / occurrence-count per signature so the UI can show new vs. recurring errors.

Done when known fixtures collapse to the expected number of signatures and masking rules are covered by tests.","tags":["errors","classification","backend"],"priority":9,"complexity":6,"estimatedHours":12}

{"workingDirectory":"/Users/fanysmacpro/Developer/agents/pe6203-agent-harness-safety/results/raw/evidence-contrastive-pilot-ready-20261102/cells/cell-005/run/workspace","projectId":"5ce92af5-1768-4313-858b-f55e1c6828ea","parentId":"d37c5c84-91c0-430b-9a88-0f3e4783af72","name":"3.4 Derive latency and traffic metrics over time windows","details":"Compute the operational metrics from the catalog (1.1) out of parsed LogEvents: request volume, throughput, error rate, and latency percentiles (p50/p95/p99) bucketed by minute/hour/day and by service/route as dimensions.

Use a percentile method that survives merging across buckets (t-digest, histogram buckets, or HDR sketch) rather than averaging pre-computed percentiles — averaging percentiles is statistically wrong and is a common dashboard bug. Handle sparse buckets and nulls explicitly.

Done when percentile output on a fixture with known distribution matches the hand-computed value within tolerance.","tags":["metrics","latency","backend"],"priority":9,"complexity":5,"estimatedHours":12}

{"workingDirectory":"/Users/fanysmacpro/Developer/agents/pe6203-agent-harness-safety/results/raw/evidence-contrastive-pilot-ready-20261102/cells/cell-005/run/workspace","projectId":"5ce92af5-1768-4313-858b-f55e1c6828ea","parentId":"d37c5c84-91c0-430b-9a88-0f3e4783af72","name":"3.5 Store log metrics with retention and rollup policy","details":"Persist log-derived MetricPoints and error signatures into the same analytical store used by the customer pipeline, using the identical MetricPoint contract from 1.2/2.5.

Define retention and rollup: keep fine-grained buckets for a short window, progressively roll up to hourly/daily for long-range views, and document the exact windows. Ensure queries over long ranges transparently select the right rollup table. Idempotent by (metric id, dimensions, bucket).

Done when a query for a 90-day range returns identically to the rolled-up source, and re-ingesting a batch does not change totals.","tags":["storage","retention","backend"],"priority":8,"complexity":4,"estimatedHours":12}

{"workingDirectory":"/Users/fanysmacpro/Developer/agents/pe6203-agent-harness-safety/results/raw/evidence-contrastive-pilot-ready-20261102/cells/cell-005/run/workspace","projectId":"5ce92af5-1768-4313-858b-f55e1c6828ea","parentId":"50905336-96c5-45dd-9bd7-a66572a34872","name":"4.1 Establish design tokens, theme, and responsive layout shell","details":"Create the visual and structural foundation all widgets inherit: color palette (including accessible, colorblind-safe categorical series), typography scale, spacing, elevation, and chart-specific tokens (grid, axis, tooltip).

Build the responsive dashboard shell: header, nav, filter bar container, and a 12-column grid that reflows between desktop/tablet/mobile. Include loading, empty, and error states as first-class components so every widget can reuse them.

Done when the shell renders at three breakpoints with placeholder cards and tokens are documented in a storybook or equivalent.","tags":["frontend","design-system","ui"],"priority":8,"complexity":4,"estimatedHours":10}

{"workingDirectory":"/Users/fanysmacpro/Developer/agents/pe6203-agent-harness-safety/results/raw/evidence-contrastive-pilot-ready-20261102/cells/cell-005/run/workspace","projectId":"5ce92af5-1768-4313-858b-f55e1c6828ea","parentId":"50905336-96c5-45dd-9bd7-a66572a34872","name":"4.2 Build core chart primitives (time series, bar, KPI tile)","details":"Implement three reusable, data-agnostic chart components: a time-series line/area chart, a categorical bar chart, and a KPI stat tile with trend/delta.

Each takes a typed props contract (series, dimensions, formatting) rather than fetching its own data, so it is pure and snapshot-testable. Cover interaction: hover tooltip with crosshair, legend toggle, and time-range brush on the time series. Handle edge cases that break naive charts: all-zero series, single data point, nulls/gaps, very long labels, and huge value ranges (axis formatting).

Done when each primitive renders from fixtures at all breakpoints and has tests for the edge cases above.","tags":["frontend","charts","components"],"priority":9,"complexity":6,"estimatedHours":16}

{"workingDirectory":"/Users/fanysmacpro/Developer/agents/pe6203-agent-harness-safety/results/raw/evidence-contrastive-pilot-ready-20261102/cells/cell-005/run/workspace","projectId":"5ce92af5-1768-4313-858b-f55e1c6828ea","parentId":"50905336-96c5-45dd-9bd7-a66572a34872","name":"4.3 Build the data table component","details":"Build the table used for drill-downs (customer lists, top error signatures): column definitions, client/server-side sorting, filtering, pagination or virtual scrolling for large result sets, and numeric/date cell formatting.

Include loading and empty states from 4.1, and a row-click hook so the table can drive cross-filtering of charts. Must stay responsive with 10k+ rows — use virtualization rather than rendering every row.

Done when it handles 10k rows smoothly, sorts and filters correctly, and edge cases (no results, single row, very wide cells) are tested.","tags":["frontend","table","components"],"priority":8,"complexity":5,"estimatedHours":10}

{"workingDirectory":"/Users/fanysmacpro/Developer/agents/pe6203-agent-harness-safety/results/raw/evidence-contrastive-pilot-ready-20261102/cells/cell-005/run/workspace","projectId":"5ce92af5-1768-4313-858b-f55e1c6828ea","parentId":"50905336-96c5-45dd-9bd7-a66572a34872","name":"4.5 Compose the customer analytics dashboard view","details":"Assemble the customer-facing view from the primitives: KPI row (active/new/returning customers, churn rate, revenue per customer), retention cohort heatmap or matrix, segment breakdown bar chart, and a customer drill-down table.

Wire all widgets to the shared filter state from 4.4 and the customer metrics from 2.4. Every widget reads from the catalog-backed definitions — no hardcoded metric logic in the UI. Include per-widget loading/empty/error states.

Done when the view renders live customer metrics, filters apply consistently to all widgets, and the numbers reconcile with 2.4's test expectations.","tags":["frontend","dashboard","customer"],"priority":8,"complexity":5,"estimatedHours":12}

{"workingDirectory":"/Users/fanysmacpro/Developer/agents/pe6203-agent-harness-safety/results/raw/evidence-contrastive-pilot-ready-20261102/cells/cell-005/run/workspace","projectId":"5ce92af5-1768-4313-858b-f55e1c6828ea","parentId":"50905336-96c5-45dd-9bd7-a66572a34872","name":"4.6 Compose the operations / log analysis dashboard view","details":"Assemble the operational view: request volume over time, error-rate trend, latency percentile chart (p50/p95/p99), and a top-error-signatures table with occurrence counts and first/last seen.

Wire to log metrics from 3.4/3.5 and error signatures from 3.3 through the shared filter state. Add cross-filtering: clicking an error signature narrows the time-series charts to that signature. Make "unparsed records" visible somewhere so silent data loss is noticeable.

Done when the view renders live log metrics, cross-filtering works, and displayed values reconcile with 3.4's percentile tests.","tags":["frontend","dashboard","operations"],"priority":8,"complexity":5,"estimatedHours":10}

{"workingDirectory":"/Users/fanysmacpro/Developer/agents/pe6203-agent-harness-safety/results/raw/evidence-contrastive-pilot-ready-20261102/cells/cell-005/run/workspace","projectId":"5ce92af5-1768-4313-858b-f55e1c6828ea","parentId":"4c9f1b23-4791-48f5-870a-b39510e77c28","name":"5.1 Write end-to-end integration tests across all three streams","details":"Prove the whole path works: CSV and log fixtures in, dashboard queries out, asserted against expected values.

Cover the seams where integration bugs live: batch boundaries, retries and idempotency, timezone handling across pipeline and UI, schema version compatibility, and filter-to-query translation. Include a golden-dataset test where the full pipeline is run and output metric values are compared to a committed expected snapshot, so unintended logic changes fail loudly.

Done when the suite runs in CI against the containerized stack and is green.","tags":["testing","integration","qa"],"priority":9,"complexity":5,"estimatedHours":12}

{"workingDirectory":"/Users/fanysmacpro/Developer/agents/pe6203-agent-harness-safety/results/raw/evidence-contrastive-pilot-ready-20261102/cells/cell-005/run/workspace","projectId":"5ce92af5-1768-4313-858b-f55e1c6828ea","parentId":"4c9f1b23-4791-48f5-870a-b39510e77c28","name":"5.2 Validate performance and load with production-scale data","details":"Use the seeded generator from 1.4 to produce production-scale CSV and log volumes, then measure and fix bottlenecks.

Establish and record targets before testing: ingestion throughput per file size, end-to-end pipeline latency, dashboard p95 query response, and dashboard first meaningful paint. Profile the slowest stage in each pipeline and the slowest dashboard query; address memory ceilings (streaming vs. load-all) and any N+1 query patterns in the API layer.

Done when documented targets are met and results are recorded with the test configuration that produced them.","tags":["performance","load-testing","qa"],"priority":8,"complexity":6,"estimatedHours":10}

{"workingDirectory":"/Users/fanysmacpro/Developer/agents/pe6203-agent-harness-safety/results/raw/evidence-contrastive-pilot-ready-20261102/cells/cell-005/run/workspace","projectId":"5ce92af5-1768-4313-858b-f55e1c6828ea","parentId":"4c9f1b23-4791-48f5-870a-b39510e77c28","name":"5.3 Set up monitoring, alerting, and operations runbooks","details":"Make the system observable in production: structured logs for both pipelines, stage-level metrics (files processed, rows rejected, parse failure rate, batch duration), and dashboard-side error tracking.

Define alerts that matter: pipeline stalled or failed, reject rate above threshold, parse failure rate above threshold, data freshness beyond SLA, and dashboard API error/latency spikes. Write runbooks for each alert with first diagnostic steps and rollback instructions.

Done when each alert fires in a staging test and has a linked runbook.","tags":["observability","alerting","ops"],"priority":8,"complexity":4,"estimatedHours":8}

{"workingDirectory":"/Users/fanysmacpro/Developer/agents/pe6203-agent-harness-safety/results/raw/evidence-contrastive-pilot-ready-20261102/cells/cell-005/run/workspace","projectId":"5ce92af5-1768-4313-858b-f55e1c6828ea","parentId":"4c9f1b23-4791-48f5-870a-b39510e77c28","name":"5.4 Write documentation and user guide","details":"Document the system for its three audiences: operators (how to run pipelines, interpret batch rejects, respond to alerts), analysts (what each metric means, its grain and freshness, where it comes from), and engineers (architecture diagram, schema versions, how to add a metric end to end).

Include a "known limitations" section — parsing formats not covered, retention windows, and any metric approximations (e.g. sketch-based percentiles). Document the exact steps to add a new CSV source or a new log format.

Done when a new team member can onboard from the docs alone and the metric definitions reconcile with the catalog.","tags":["documentation","enablement"],"priority":6,"complexity":3,"estimatedHours":6}
